3 finding(s): 3 to consider; 2 on their lines. Reply in a comment's thread to answer it.

### Outside the diff

- 🟡🐛 **Consider · bug: holdOwnDraft still ignores a file-only draft, so Enter can be dropped in the receipt-pending window (confidence low)** (`frontend/src/renderer/components/chat/ChatComposer.tsx:1831`): This PR makes Enter on a file-only box count as a new message when a send is in flight (line 1775, `textRef.current.trim() || nextDraftHasFiles()`). The sibling path `holdOwnDraft` (line 1831) still returns false unless there is text. `performSubmit` calls it at line 1850 when the previous send was accepted but its receipt has not been applied yet (`beginChatComposerMutation` returned no token and nothing is pending). A file-only Enter pressed in that one-commit window is silently dropped. The same Enter with text would be held and sent. Is the asymmetry intended? If not, `holdOwnDraft` could use the same `textRef.current.trim() || nextDraftHasFiles()` test. The user can press Enter again, so the cost is small.

### Summary

I found three minor issues, none blocking. I only read the code and did not run the tests. The core logic holds up. Staging waits for any tracked restore and applies the same `assertRestored` as the send path. Sent files are dropped from the box on accept and on park, while next-message files are kept. The new tests match what the code does. The three issues:
- `holdOwnDraft` still ignores a file-only draft, so a file-only Enter can be dropped in the one-commit window after a send is accepted.
- In `useStageAttachments` the restore wait now runs before `toWireAttachments`, so a restore that starts during that step is not awaited.
- The comment explaining the archived-session stager gate in `SessionChatSurface.tsx` was deleted, and this diff contains no code change to that gate.

The PR body also says the composer takes next files "only when the message being sent has no files of its own". The code and tests allow next files while the sent message has files, so the body is out of date.

