--- frontend/src/renderer/hooks/useConversation.ts:2428 ---
👮 **Wachiman** · 🟡🐛 **Consider · bug: Restore wait now runs before the wire conversion, so a restore that starts during it is not awaited (confidence low)**

The old code awaited the in-flight restore after `toWireAttachments`, right before the POST. The new code awaits it once, before `toWireAttachments` (lines 2428-2432). The wait is skipped when no restore is tracked at call time. If a restore starts while `toWireAttachments` is reading or uploading a large file, for example from the Restore button or another window, the POST at line 2433 goes to the archived session before its worktree is back. That is the case the old order covered. Moving the wait before the wire step does keep a large upload from starting early. Awaiting `restoreInFlight` a second time just before the POST would cover both orders.

<!-- wachi:finding -->
--- frontend/src/renderer/components/chat/SessionChatSurface.tsx:953 ---
👮 **Wachiman** · 🟡📝 **Consider · docs: Comment explaining the archived-session stager gate was deleted (confidence medium)**

The only change in this file is deleting the two-line comment above `onStageAttachments`. The condition on line 953 is unchanged. The comment said why the stager is offered only while the session is active or `commands.resumingAgent` is true: the worktree is gone until the restore runs. Nothing in the PR makes that explanation untrue, and the gate is easy to misread without it. The PR body also lists a gate change in this file as part of the fix, but this diff has none. Please keep the comment, or say in the PR which commit changed the gate.

